# Multi-Campus Architecture

InstitutionKit is engineered from the ground up as a **multi-tenant ERP** — not a single-school system with multiple locations bolted on. A single WordPress installation powers unlimited campuses, each with complete data isolation, independent financial tracking, and role-based access control enforced at the database query layer.

---

## Core Philosophy

Most "multi-campus" school systems simply add a dropdown filter. InstitutionKit implements **true multi-tenancy**:

| Principle | Implementation |
|-----------|---------------|
| **Data Isolation** | Every table includes `campus_id` as a partition key. Queries are filtered before execution, not after. |
| **Role-Bound Visibility** | Campus Admins cannot query data outside their campus. This is SQL-level enforcement, not UI-hiding. |
| **Independent Configuration** | Fee structures, expense heads, grading scales, and operating hours can differ per campus. |
| **Aggregated Intelligence** | Super Admins toggle between single-campus views and cross-campus analytics. Zero-config aggregation. |
| **Audit Trail** | Every campus transfer is logged with timestamps, actor IDs, and reasons — permanent, immutable history. |

---

## Two-Tier Administration Model

InstitutionKit implements a binary privilege model — there is no "partial multi-campus" access. A user is either **sovereign** (all campuses) or **bound** (single campus).

=== "Super Admin"

    | Property | Value |
    |----------|-------|
    | WordPress Role | `administrator` |
    | Campus Scope | All campuses + "All Campuses" aggregate |
    | Switching | Admin bar, dashboard dropdown, URL parameter |
    | Capabilities | All 62 custom capabilities |
    | Data Access | Unfiltered — sees everything |

    !!! success "Power User Feature"
        When viewing "All Campuses" (`campus_id=0`), the system returns aggregated financial summaries, combined attendance statistics, and cross-campus comparison tables. This is not a sum of individual queries — it's a single optimized aggregation pass.

=== "Campus Admin"

    | Property | Value |
    |----------|-------|
    | WordPress Role | `campus_admin` only (must NOT also be `administrator`) |
    | Campus Scope | Single assigned campus — locked |
    | Switching | No switcher visible. Cannot override via URL. |
    | Capabilities | 48 campus-scoped capabilities |
    | Data Access | SQL-filtered to `campus_id = [their_campus]` |

    !!! danger "Critical Security Rule"
        If a user holds **both** `administrator` and `campus_admin` roles, the `administrator` role takes precedence and the user becomes a Super Admin with unrestricted access. The system checks: `in_array('campus_admin', $roles) && !in_array('administrator', $roles)`.

